  "description": "Tony Donnelly of Leonard Wilson Keenan is proud to present Rathview House.\n\nThis substantial, c. 4,160 sq. ft. three-storey-over-basement period residence dates back to the early 1800s. A protected structure, the property retains magnificent original features, including the ornate cast-iron front gate and railings.\nThe Residence\nBeyond its imposing double-fronted facade lies a spacious entrance hallway, flanked by two grand reception rooms and a formal dining room to the rear. The elegant staircase leads to the first floor, which hosts three extensive bedrooms and a family bathroom, all enjoying superb views over the rear grounds. The second floor offers a further four generous double bedrooms.\n\nThe Basement & Grounds\n\nThe expansive basement is currently configured as a kitchen and three storerooms, offering a myriad of opportunities for conversion, a home business, or self-contained living (subject to planning). Outside, a private side entrance leads to a mature, extra-large, south-facing rear garden—a true sun trap.\nThe Location\nCommandingly positioned at the top of the village, Rathview House is within walking distance of Rathangan town centre, the Grand Canal Blueway, the Slate River, and local schools. The M7 motorway, The Curragh Racecourse, and Kildare Village Outlet are all just a short drive away.\n\nKey Information:\n•\tHeating: Oil-Fired & Solid Fuel\n•\tWater: Mains Supply\n•\tWaste: Septic Tank\n•\tBER Exempt\n\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***",
